    "result_text": "The full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the rule: creating an owner is rejected with **409 Conflict** when the owner's city already contains 50 or more owners.\n\nTo keep structural impact low, I added the behaviour as small, cohesive units rather than growing any existing method:\n\n1. **New file `OwnerCityCapacityPolicy.java`** \u2014 a self-contained policy (mirroring the existing `OwnerTelephonePolicy`/`OwnerNamesakePolicy` pattern) that counts existing owners in the candidate's city and throws a `CityAtCapacityException` (annotated `@ResponseStatus(CONFLICT)`) at the threshold of 50.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 one added call plus one import. The check runs on the owner's mapped city before save.\n\n3. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 a small new `@ExceptionHandler` method (needed because the class's catch-all `@ExceptionHandler(Exception.class)` otherwise turns the exception into a 500, exactly as the sibling policies each have their own handler).\n\nAll complexity lives in the new class; the edits to existing (larger) classes are each a single simple line/method, keeping per-function cost minimal.",
